  </question>

  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>Q06: Stack vs Queue Code Analysis</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>You have an empty data structure. You perform the following:</p>
<pre><code>add(1)
add(2)
add(3)
val = remove()
print(val)</code></pre>
<p>If the result is <strong>1</strong>, which data structure was used?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>If the first item added (1) is the first item removed, it is a Queue (FIFO).</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0</defaultgrade>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Queue]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Stack]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Sorted List]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Recursive Tree]]></text></answer>
  </question>

  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>Q07: Linked List Insertion: Head</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>What is the primary advantage of inserting a node at the <strong>Head</strong> of a linked list compared to an array?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Linked lists only need to update pointers, while arrays must shift every single element to the right.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0</defaultgrade>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[It is instant and does not require shifting elements.]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[It automatically sorts the rest of the list.]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[It uses less memory than inserting at the tail.]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[It allows direct index access to the new node.]]></text></answer>
  </question>

  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>Q08: Recursive Countdown Output</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>What does the following code print?</p>
<pre><code>def countdown(n):
    if n <= 0:
        print("Done")
        return
    print(n, end=" ")
    countdown(n - 1)

countdown(2)</code></pre>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>1. n=2: print 2, call countdown(1). 2. n=1: print 1, call countdown(0). 3. n=0: print Done.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0</defaultgrade>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[2 1 Done]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[1 2 Done]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[2 1 0 Done]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Done 1 2]]></text></answer>
  </question>

